      <CodeBlock code={"$ curl --cacert cacert.crt <secret_manifest_url> -H \\\n\"x-kubevirt-export-token:token_decode\" -H \\\n\"Accept:application/yaml\""} lang="terminal" />
      <ul>
      <li>Replace <code>&lt;secret_manifest_url&gt;</code> with an <code>auth-header-secret</code> URL from the <code>VirtualMachineExport</code> YAML output.</li>
      <li>
      Reference the <code>token_decode</code> file that you created earlier.
      <p>For example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ curl --cacert cacert.crt https://vmexport-proxy.test.net/api/export.kubevirt.io/v1beta1/namespaces/example/virtualmachineexports/example-export/external/manifests/secret -H \"x-kubevirt-export-token:token_decode\" -H \"Accept:application/yaml\""} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
      Get the manifests of <code>type: all</code>, such as the <code>ConfigMap</code> and <code>VirtualMachine</code> manifests, by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ curl --cacert cacert.crt <all_manifest_url> -H \\\n\"x-kubevirt-export-token:token_decode\" -H \\\n\"Accept:application/yaml\""} lang="terminal" />
      <ul>
      <li>Replace <code>&lt;all_manifest_url&gt;</code> with a URL from the <code>VirtualMachineExport</code> YAML output.</li>
      <li>
      Reference the <code>token_decode</code> file that you created earlier.
      <p>For example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ curl --cacert cacert.crt https://vmexport-proxy.test.net/api/export.kubevirt.io/v1beta1/namespaces/example/virtualmachineexports/example-export/external/manifests/all -H \"x-kubevirt-export-token:token_decode\" -H \"Accept:application/yaml\""} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Next steps</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You can now create the <code>ConfigMap</code> and <code>VirtualMachine</code> objects on the target cluster by using the exported manifests.</li></ul>
